##############################################################################
# Tools database used to build the toolcall.f subroutine
#
# RCS:  ProMAX $Id: tools.db 44084 2009-03-24 21:43:10Z Steven M Cook $ $Revision: 44084 $ $Date: 2009-03-24 15:43:10 -0600 (Tue, 24 Mar 2009) $
#
##############################################################################
# The "label" field contains the character string used to determine which
# tool is called.  The "entry" field contains the entry point of the
# tool's subroutines, but without the INIT_ or EXEC_ parts.  Note that
# both label and entry must be UPPERCASE by convention, although, in this
# database, entry may be "same" for those tools (most tools) for which
# label and entry are the same.
#
# The "type" field contains the tool's type, such as "simple" or
# "complex".  The optional "conditional" field is used to describe
# conditions under which the tool is to be included.  The syntax of this
# field is the same as that used in an #if directive to the C
# pre-processor.
#
# The "library" field indicates whether a tool is a part of the libmaxtool'n'
# libraries that is 'internal' or whether the tool is built into a separate
# shared object (library) that is named in this column.
##############################################################################

